# The appointment manager's block for the CHATBOT's Caddyfile
# (chatbotasesor_multicliente/deploy/Caddyfile; on the VPS,
# /srv/chatbot/deploy/Caddyfile). It goes at the end, after the instances.
#
# It reuses that file's `(instancia)` snippet, which already does all that is
# needed and was tested in the chatbot's phase 5:
#   - `header_up X-Forwarded-For {http.request.header.CF-Connecting-IP}`
#     REPLACES the header. Without it anyone could forge their IP and skip the
#     per-IP limits of booking and of the link (D-007). The app believes the
#     first hop of X-Forwarded-For because TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS is not empty.
#   - `reverse_proxy <name>:3000`, `encode`, and dropping `Server`.
# The security headers (HSTS, CSP…) are the app's own.
#
# The domain comes from a variable, like the chatbot's, in /srv/chatbot/caddy.env:
#   GESTOR_CITAS_DOMINIO=niza.automatizacionro.work
# One level only: Cloudflare's free certificate does not cover two.
#
# When it moves to the client's domain, the old one redirects keeping the path,
# so the links in emails already sent keep working:
#   {$GESTOR_CITAS_DOMINIO_ANTERIOR} {
#   	redir https://{$GESTOR_CITAS_DOMINIO}{uri} permanent
#   }

{$GESTOR_CITAS_DOMINIO} {
	import instancia gestor-citas-app
}
